# API services

`apps/<app>/src/utils/services/` wraps backend endpoints only: method, URL, typed request/response.

Use the app axios instance (`api` from `@dv-admin/utils/libs/axios`, `@pay/utils/libs/axios`, or `@pay-simple/utils/libs/axios`). Name functions `getApi…` / `postApi…` / `putApi…` / `deleteApi…`. Return `resp.data.data` (or void for empty bodies).

Do **not** put defaults, filter merging, pagination, mapping, or other call-site logic in a service. That belongs in the store, component, or composable that calls it.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — defaults and filter assembly in the service
export const getApiAmlHistory = async (page?: number) => {
	const resp = await api.get("/dv-admin/aml/history", {
		params: { page: page ?? 1, per_page: 20 }
	});
	return resp.data.data;
};

// ✅ GOOD — pass through what the caller sends
export const getApiAmlHistory = async (params: IAmlHistoryFilterRequest): Promise<IAmlHistoryResponse> => {
	const resp = await api.get("/dv-admin/aml/history", { params });
	return resp.data.data;
};
```

Path params that are part of the URL (`/dv-admin/aml/${slug}/keys`) stay in the service signature. Query `page` / `filters` are passed in by the caller.
